From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yassine Oudjana <y.oudjana@protonmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:44:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: dsi: Register DSI host after preparing
 everything

Currently mipi_dsi_host_register is the first thing called on probe,
making DRM try to access it before anything is prepared. Move registering
the DSI host to the end to ensure it is accessed only after everything is
ready.

Signed-off-by: Yassine Oudjana <y.oudjana@protonmail.com>
[Patrick: rebased onto v7.0, where the driver data is already set
 before registration; from linux-mediatek mt6789-next a332e9128dfd]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c | 18 ++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
index 26de9ee5..d86cc994 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
@@ -1236,27 +1236,25 @@ static int mtk_dsi_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (irq_num < 0)
 		return irq_num;
 
-	dsi->host.ops = &mtk_dsi_ops;
-	dsi->host.dev = dev;
-
 	init_waitqueue_head(&dsi->irq_wait_queue);
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, dsi);
 
-	ret = mipi_dsi_host_register(&dsi->host);
-	if (ret < 0)
-		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Failed to register DSI host\n");
-
 	ret = devm_request_irq(&pdev->dev, irq_num, mtk_dsi_irq,
 			       IRQF_TRIGGER_NONE, dev_name(&pdev->dev), dsi);
-	if (ret) {
-		mipi_dsi_host_unregister(&dsi->host);
+	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, ret, "Failed to request DSI irq\n");
-	}
 
 	dsi->bridge.of_node = dev->of_node;
 	dsi->bridge.type = DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DSI;
 
+	dsi->host.ops = &mtk_dsi_ops;
+	dsi->host.dev = dev;
+
+	ret = mipi_dsi_host_register(&dsi->host);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Failed to register DSI host\n");
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
